    "problem_statement": "A UDP socket's open operation must take the network interface identifier it will be bound to as part of opening, rather than relying on the bind call to supply it. Opening a UDP socket on the Thread network interface (and binding it to a port) must associate the socket with that interface so the bind validates against the correct interface. Code that opens a UDP socket and then binds it to a port on a specific interface must, after opening, record the requested interface on the socket before binding.",
